      "writtenOn": "2016-10-14T18:40:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both Reef\u0027s TCPC stop toggling once something is plugged in and will resume toggling when it is unplugged.\n\nSince it is resuming back to PD_STATE_SNK/SRC_DISCONNECTED, calling tcpm_set_cc and other variables will make sure the state of the TCPC/TCPM is identical as if the DRP auto toggle is not used.\n\nAnother reason is mentioned in tcpci.c regarding Rp should set to lowest during DRP auto toggle and restore to the expected Rp when a SRC device is plugged in.",
      "parentUuid": "fc2ec625_e428248e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2738,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 2738,
        "endChar": 35
      },
