        "id": 1111479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-14T18:40:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, I do see a bug.\n\nIf a SNK is plugged during PD_STATE_DRP_TOGGLE, power_role is PD_ROLE_SINK in line 2736, so this will not get executed because of line 2777; continue to PD_STATE_SNK_DISCONNECTED, but if a unplug happens before it gets to PD_STATE_SNK_DISCONNECTED_DEBOUNCE, then it will go back to manual DRP toggle since PD_FLAGS_TCPC_DRP_TOGGLE is not cleared.\n\nIf a SRC is plugged during PD_STATE_DRP_TOGGLE and state connected, this will be skipped also because of line 2782; but same thing that if a unplug happens before PD_STATE_SRC_DISCONNECTED_DEBOUNCE, then it will go back to manual DRP toggle also.\n\nIf a quick (msec?) unplug happened before it even get to PD_STATE_SRC_DISCONNECTED, PD_FLAGS_TCPC_DRP_TOGGLE will be set initially to indicate we just came out of toggle in line 2742, but when line 2800 is called, last state is already PD_STATE_SRC_DISCONNECTED, and next state is PD_STATE_SNK_DISCONNECTED, then PD_FLAGS_TCPC_DRP_TOGGLE will not get clear and go back to manual DRP toggle.\n\nWe have discussed about a plug/unplug automated test, will PM you for more details.",
      "parentUuid": "fc2ec625_643df4c4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2792,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 2792,
        "endChar": 25
      },
